{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1118","id":4810209650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABHrX5cg","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1118","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1118.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1118.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1118","number":1118,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"30004231: accepted counterexamples for totally mixed face posets","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Accepted complete negative answer and published preprint\n\nBoth assertions in Sam Payne's printed OWR39/2019 p2464 Problem 3 are false under its positive canonical summand dimensions and full dimension-additivity condition. For the full-dimensional lattice polytopes D4×[0,1] and (-D4)×[0,1] in R5, the qualifying-face order complex is two connected pure graphs, each with 50 vertices and 60 edges. Its rational Betti numbers are (2,22,0,...); it is nonshellable and fails the printed sphere-wedge homology assertion. The shared interval is deliberate. This concerns the literal printed question; different generic/stable tropical intersection definitions remain outside the claim.\n\nPublished preprint: **Negative answers to the printed totally mixed face questions**, Alec Kriebel, version 1.0.0 (2026-10-17), [DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23440943](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440943). The record contains the four-page self-contained note and the source/verification archive with two independent exact standard-library programs and supporting audits. Zenodo readback verified the exact reviewed files and metadata, with no normalization; the DOI resolves. The Google Workspace tracker entry at **Math Puzzles!A153:D153** was appended once and read back exactly.\n\nRoot and independent geometry/topology adversaries reproduced the complete face classification, all 543 nonempty faces and 8,649 summand-face pairs, graph incidences, signed rational boundaries and shellability controls. The extended priority audit records 109 distinct queries and 20 source/version records. Classical Fukuda–Weibel geometry and Sturmfels–Tevelev's six-point antecedent are credited; the different Adiprasito definitions and current Hiatt–Simpson–Wang–Wu v2 tropical counterexample are distinguished. No prior exact-target nonshellability result or verified implication was identified. This is a bounded audit, not a worldwide novelty certificate: the paywalled final body of Adiprasito's 2024 article was not inspected, and this limit is explicit throughout the package.\n\nThe first fresh whole-package review caught a missing current literature revision. All operative source comparisons, citations, metadata and archives were repaired and rebuilt. Two NEW successive fresh whole-package reviewers then passed the identical repaired package with no actionable findings; the final reviewer had no inherited conversation history. They independently checked mathematics and adverse controls, primary source/version claims, all archives and metadata, standalone verification in normal/optimized modes, and all four pages' rebuilt text, drawing streams, pixels and visual layout. [Review evidence and repair history](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/main/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1118_30004231).\n\nAI tools were used extensively in development, verification, research and writing. The preprint is **unrefereed**; AI adversarial review is not external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification.\n\nAccepted source head: `8592fb7297d3c4973f2778c47cfa8972cba896a6`. The accepted publication package and review history are already checkpointed on main. Merge only this exact reviewed PR head.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T09:29:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T19:05:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b7f82168f93056813f74f3078d6f0a0cdd0fb5fd","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1118/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1118/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1118/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/8592fb7297d3c4973f2778c47cfa8972cba896a6","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:publication/30004231-totally-mixed-faces-negative","ref":"publication/30004231-totally-mixed-faces-negative","sha":"8592fb7297d3c4973f2778c47cfa8972cba896a6","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.